WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.860
- You're going to learn some tips

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.630
to speak clearly and confidently.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:04.463
Specifically,

00:00:04.463 --> 00:00:06.900
you'll learn how to speak
with more conviction.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.540
This is part five in a five part series

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.760
on "How to Speak Clearly and Confidently."

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.230
This is the last video

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:16.440
and it's 100% compatible
with every other lesson

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.820
and tip in the series.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.530
If you've been watching the series

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.600
and still haven't subscribed yet,

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.130
then you can do that right now

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.840
and if you're finding
these lessons helpful,

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.320
then feel free to check out my
Communication Coach Academy.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.791
We have loads of free resources there,

00:00:30.791 --> 00:00:32.910
group coaching options

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.340
and a variety of classes
and communication,

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.170
public speaking and leadership.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.020
Today's video is all about
speaking with conviction

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.290
and the bottom line is if
you have something to say,

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.123
say it like you mean it.

00:00:45.123 --> 00:00:48.330
Tip number one, to speak
with more conviction

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:51.210
is to increase your volume.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.340
I would say that more
than half of the clients

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.130
I work with do not speak loudly enough

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:59.280
in group situations or
during presentations.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.120
The trouble is,

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.540
people who speak softly
generally do not sound confident

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:04.860
in what they're saying.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.680
If you speak at a below average volume,

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:10.980
it's going to create a
below average impression.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:11.813
In contrast,

00:01:11.813 --> 00:01:14.957
if you can increase your
volume by just 10 or 20%,

00:01:14.957 --> 00:01:18.180
everything you say will
sound more enthusiastic

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.500
and committed.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.390
If you're in a one-on-one
conversation of course,

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:25.020
you have to keep the level
of volume conversational,

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.720
but in front of a group
of almost any size,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.780
increase your volume by about 10 or 20%.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.430
For public speaking the tip

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.710
is to let your voice fill the room.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.650
The larger the room and the
more people that are there,

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:40.080
the more volume you use.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.670
When you speak a little louder,

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.470
it'll make everything you say,

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.630
like you're speaking with conviction.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:46.710
When I work with clients,

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.360
we'll often do this in workshops

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.600
with somebody who is speaking
too softly for the room.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.580
They volunteer and we put them up there

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.570
in front of everybody.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:55.793
We're really supportive

00:01:55.793 --> 00:01:59.100
and we gradually get them to speak louder.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.440
And you can try this with me right now

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.380
and I'm going to use a sample
sentence about pickleball

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.810
from a previous lesson in this series.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.910
We'll gradually increase the volume

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.740
and it's just a pickleball,

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:13.260
but you'll see how this
makes a difference.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.850
Repeat the sentence after me
in your normal speaking volume.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:21.153
Pickleball is now one of the
most popular sports around.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.130
Now, let's say that again,

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:26.400
and this time let's speak 10% louder

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.850
and let your voice start to
fill whatever room you're in.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:33.720
Pickleball is now one of the
most popular sports around.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.850
Now, let's increase the
volume one more time

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:39.060
to 20% higher than your normal volume

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.740
and say it again with me.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:44.820
Pickleball is now one of the
most popular sports around.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:45.750
Now, I'm not there with you,

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.219
but I'm willing to speculate

00:02:47.219 --> 00:02:49.470
that when you speak a little louder,

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:51.390
you'll sound more confident

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.940
and convinced about what you just said.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.210
You may also notice as you
practice speaking louder,

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.170
that you're benefiting

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.840
from a few other positive side effects.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:01.860
I've noticed that

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.710
when most of my clients
increase their volume,

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.380
they also increase their vocal variety

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.460
in the sound of their voice.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.530
So, they no longer sound monotone.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.530
That's because increasing
your volume naturally,

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.960
improves your tone and inflection.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.870
My clients also usually
start to become more animated

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.240
in terms of their gestures
in their body language

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.800
and their facial expressions.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.750
I can't obviously see you right now,

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.580
but let me ask, did you notice

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.700
that your facial expressions
became more animated

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.590
when you increased your volume?

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:35.250
Did you gesture with your
hands without realizing it?

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.040
All of that will make you
come across as more confident

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.390
in what you're saying.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:42.000
So, all you have to do
is increase your volume

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.740
by about 10% or 20%

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.260
and you'll look and sound
like you're speaking

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.699
with more conviction.

00:03:47.699 --> 00:03:50.488
Tip number two to speak
with more conviction

00:03:50.488 --> 00:03:55.470
is to emphasize the most
important words in each sentence.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.690
In fact, I just did that
in my previous sentence,

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:58.920
so I'll do it again

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.070
and you tell me which words I emphasized.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.540
To speak with more conviction,

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:07.950
emphasize the most important
words in each sentence.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:09.120
Did you hear it?

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.410
And you can do the same.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:14.220
All I did was slow down and
lean into what I consider

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.350
to be the most important words,

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:19.470
and you should do that
in every single sentence.

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:22.410
Just pick whatever two
or three words in a row

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:23.910
that matter the most in each sentence.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.940
Slow down and add emphasis to them.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:30.030
There are lots of reasons
to emphasize key words.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:32.400
The first is that when
people speak too rapidly

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.890
and rush through every
thought and every sentence,

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:36.330
it doesn't sound confident.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:39.450
It sounds like they're just
trying to get through a message

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:42.120
and their main goal is
to get it over with.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.270
Now, rushing through may
help you accomplish the goal

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:47.460
of finishing as fast as possible,

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.140
but it's not going to make you sound,

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.300
like you believe what you're saying.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.470
Another reason people rush is
because of anxiety and nerves,

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:58.020
but whatever reason you have
for speaking too quickly,

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.870
emphasizing the most
important words in each

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:02.640
and every sentence will give you

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:05.250
a much more confident sounding rhythm.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.390
It also helps your listeners,

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:07.854
because now they know

00:05:07.854 --> 00:05:10.140
that if it's important
to you as a speaker,

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:12.990
then you're signaling that it
should be important to them.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:15.030
And here's another tip within a tip.

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:17.430
When you get to the end
of your talking turn,

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:20.220
make sure you use the
same type of emphasis

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:23.190
on the last three words you say

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:26.490
and make sure your voice
goes down at the end,

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:29.040
toward the period punctuation mark.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.470
It should sound like you
are landing the plane

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:32.940
on your talking turn.

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:34.920
Let's use our pickleball example again

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.360
and say it along with me.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:39.450
We'll pretend that this is
the end of our talking turn.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:42.270
Emphasize the last three
words as you read this

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.790
and notice how certain you sound.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:48.990
Pickleball is now one of the
most popular sports around.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.150
You really wanna lean into
those last three words.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.940
Make sure it sounds like
you're making a statement

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.190
and not asking a question.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:58.230
Third, let's talk eye contact

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.970
and how you can use this

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:01.740
to come across as more confident,

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:04.470
like you really believe
what you just said.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:05.580
Before I give you this tip,

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:08.100
let me explain how I learned this myself.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.710
I've been going to group
meetings as a participant

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.050
and coaching clients for decades now

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:15.660
and I've noticed a very subtle behavior

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:18.360
that differentiates the
most confident speakers

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.400
from everybody else in the room.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.870
First and most obviously,

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:24.540
confident speakers tend
to make direct eye contact

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.280
with people as they're speaking.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:28.890
That's probably not too surprising

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:31.020
and I would guess like most people,

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:33.750
you make at least some direct eye contact

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.580
when you're speaking, but if you don't,

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.961
make sure you practice eye contact,

00:06:37.961 --> 00:06:40.230
while you're speaking
and sharing your message.

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.063
A second,

00:06:41.063 --> 00:06:44.340
here's the subtle difference
I noticed about eye contact.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.670
When the most confident speakers
finish their talking turns,

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.724
they keep their eyes and their chin up

00:06:50.724 --> 00:06:54.660
and they continue to make eye
contact with the next person

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:56.280
in the group who speaks.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:59.640
They don't stare or
glare at the next person

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:00.930
in a confrontational way.

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:05.100
They simply maintain eye contact
with whoever speaks next.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.670
In contrast, professionals
who seem to lack confidence

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:09.840
in what they said,

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.960
finish their talking turn
and then they drop their eyes

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.820
and their chin toward the table,

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:17.040
toward their notes or toward a device.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.900
And when they break eye contact like that

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:20.670
and look down after they speak,

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:23.640
it creates the impression
that they don't believe in

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:26.250
or stand behind what they just said.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.390
To reiterate the tip,

00:07:27.390 --> 00:07:30.480
when you finish your talking
turn in a group situation,

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.190
keep your chin up,

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:35.520
maintain eye contact
with whoever speaks next

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:38.070
and it will cast a very positive light

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:39.840
on what you just said

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:43.385
and it'll come across like
you stand behind your message.

00:07:43.385 --> 00:07:46.050
If you watched all five
videos in this series

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:48.090
on how to speak clearly and confidently,

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:49.920
please let me know in a comment.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:53.040
I would love to celebrate that
with you with my own comment,

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.780
and I will give you a heart.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:57.000
And don't forget to take
a look at my website.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.030
There's free resources
there that I mentioned,

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.910
group coaching options and classes.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:04.950
Thank you for joining me in this journey.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:05.940
Until next time, thanks.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:07.690
God bless, and I will see you soon.

